Erik wrote:
> I found a wand of polymorph in minetown and turned my cat into a pit
> fiend.  Handy little bugger, but it killed a co-aligned priest in the
> minetown temple.  Do I suffer any penalty for this?  Can I still
> sacrifice at the altar safely (not the priest, of course)?  Also,
> speaking as one who has NEVER ascended (despite playing on and off for
> a depressingly long time), am I completely screwed by my inability to
> donate my way to a lower AC?
>
No, you suffer no penalty for what your pets do.  You can certainly
sacrifice safely at the altar.  Whenever you enter the temple room, you
will get a message related to the death of the priest, and there is a
chance that a ghost will be generated; but that has to do with you
entering the room, not sacrificing or praying.

There is at least one other guaranteed priest for you to donate to, but
you may very well need AC long before you can get there. However, there
is at least one other, priestless, supernatural way to lower your AC.



